    docs(s3): document effective-endpoint precedence for env overrides (DOC-3)
    
    DOGFOOD-030 (6f6ce66) made `s3 status`/`s3 sync`/`s3 query` resolve the
    endpoint env-first via resolveEffectiveEndpoint, but the docs still named only
    the config key, so env-configured MinIO/Hetzner deployments read the wrong
    endpoint.
    
    Documented both resolved chains and the asymmetry between them:
    - Path A (in-process): AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3 -> AWS_ENDPOINT_URL -> s3.endpoint
      -> AWS default
    - Path B (push child, git-remote-s3/botocore via buildPushEnv): config
      s3.endpoint is injected as AWS_ENDPOINT_URL and spread after process.env, so
      it REPLACES the operator's own AWS_ENDPOINT_URL; only AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3
      passes through both paths.
    
    Measured live 2026-09-20 against botocore 1.42.59 with the shipped config
    value, plus a credentials-free reproducer. README synopsis corrected to match;
    buildPushEnv paragraph corrected (endpoint no longer described as deriving from
    config alone).
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
